  "limits": [
    "Dance cycles low/high/fixed-midpoint-forward per accepted batch; overflow preserves the phase and endpoint.",
    "The midpoint is computed from the missing envelope once per invocation, adds at most one gap and bounds active work reservations at three.",
    "Lane direction follows each batch; concurrent GPU lanes do not promise serial wall-clock execution.",
    "Canonical receipts permit restart with any supported order or geometry. Restart rebuilds the pivot and starts low.",
    "No kernel arithmetic, persisted job/configuration/schema/protocol/capability change. Existing minikeys-v1 workers remain compatible.",
    "Both lengths and all encodings are tested. Eight-device spots alternate lengths; no full device-by-length product or fleet scaling claim.",
    "Eleven focused host ASan/UBSan gates; no whole-application or device-code sanitizer claim.",
